{
  "about": "Parity cases for classes. Member cases run on FIXTURES (the oracle serializes each recipe object, every runner decodes the identical object); construct:true cases instead build the object with each binding's own API, to test construction itself. Cases (native-backed: the .NET oracle needs librhino3dm_native). Objects are built from recipes each runner evaluates in its own language: {\"new\": T, \"args\": [...]}, {\"call\": \"T.Static\", \"args\": [...]}, {\"on\": obj, \"call\": \"Method\", \"args\": [...]}, {\"Point3dList\": [[x,y,z], ...]}, {\"enum\": \"Type.Value\"}. \"type\" names the class whose member is under test (the generated runner wraps the object as <type>X). Results: out-parameters come back as a list [return, out1, ...]; class instances as {\"class\": name}.",
